  <prompt>Prove the 11 acceptance items of the child-record contract live on dev with a BU member (U-BU) and a secure-root sharee (U-S), using zz- test rows that are cleaned up.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE engineer running a live security gate.</role>
  <goal>Each of the 11 items has a recorded pass with evidence (row ids, owner ids, caller results); failures are fixed or filed before 035 completes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Contract §5 (git show origin/work/unified-access-control-r2:projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/ontology-standard-child-contract-2026-10-12.md). Live seam test conventions: SIGNALS_LIVE_DATAVERSE_URL / SIGNALS_LIVE_CALLER_ID (current-task.md), AzureCliCredential, zz- prefix cleanup.</background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Dev data writes are limited to zz- rows created and deleted by the gate (owner approval for the run is required before starting). No role or schema changes. Record results in notes/146-live-gate.md and hand them to the main session for uac-r2's batch5 live-gates note.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm every gate precondition in metadata; if any is unmet, STOP.</step>
    <step order="2">Run items 1-11 in order; capture evidence per item.</step>
    <step order="3">Clean up zz- rows; verify counts are 0.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any item failing on a real leak (a caller reads a row they must not) → STOP, record, escalate per root CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Items 1-11 of contract §5 each recorded as pass with evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">uac-r2 K-c (#1665): the writer identity's AppendTo on contact lets a DR with sprk_assignedtointernal be written live (evidence: row id + writer identity).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">#1780 K1: notes/146-live-gate.md and deployment guide §10.5 state that the 140 schema (DR sprk_regarding* columns) must reach an environment before any BFF containing UAC 182's DR lineage row; SecureChildShareSynchronizer / SecureChildReconciliationJob select those columns without a probe, so a missing column fails the whole secure-child load.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All zz- rows removed (query shows 0).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

